{"evt":"note_created","id":"note-mqefrogaql8","workspace":"/Users/imyu/Desktop/zonoid","title":"Legacy edge re-judge calibration pilot: LLM prune rate 24% vs 43% cosine proxy — proxy massively overestimates","summary":"Task #30 pilot adjudicated 100 legacy kept edges (50 from proxy-prune stratum cos<0.55, 50 from proxy-keep stratum cos>=0.55) with full neighborhood-aware LLM reasoning.\n\nSAMPLE: 1660 total legacy kept edges; 1122 evaluable (both endpoints have vecs), 538 no-vec. Proxy at 0.55: 725 would-prune, 397 would-keep. Stratified sample: n=50 proxy-prune, n=50 proxy-keep.\n\nLLM VERDICTS:\n- Proxy-prune stratum: LLM prune=19/50 (38%), LLM keep=31/50 (62%)\n- Proxy-keep stratum: LLM prune=5/50 (10%), LLM keep=45/50 (90%)\n\nCONFUSION MATRIX (proxy rows, LLM cols):\n  proxy-prune→LLM-prune: 19  proxy-prune→LLM-keep: 31\n  proxy-keep→LLM-prune: 5   proxy-keep→LLM-keep: 45\n\nOVERALL SAMPLE LLM prune rate: 24/100 = 24.0%\nPOPULATION-WEIGHTED ESTIMATE: 0.646×0.38 + 0.354×0.10 = 28.1% of evaluable; ~19% of all 1660 legacy edges.\n\nKEY FINDING: Cosine proxy at 0.55 predicts 42.9% prune rate; real LLM judge estimates ~24-28%. Proxy OVERESTIMATES prune rate by ~15-19 percentage points — the cosine-era edges are semantically closer in context than raw embedding cosine suggests. The proxy would prune ~315-370 more edges than the LLM actually would out of 1122 evaluable.\n\nRECOMMENDATION: GO on full re-adjudication, but do NOT use the proxy to filter — run the full LLM judge via markForRejudge. The proxy is not trustworthy as a standalone estimator (false-prune rate 62% in prune stratum). The true LLM prune rate is likely 19-28% of evaluable, meaning ~213-315 edges warrant pruning out of 1660 legacy kept.","created_by":"main","valid_from":"2026-06-14T23:49:22.954Z","vec":[-0.013393568806350231,0.041348885744810104,-0.05791628733277321,-0.02216256409883499,0.06318148225545883,-0.020325547084212303,-0.05013474076986313,0.031857628375291824,-0.09136953949928284,0.0343759